{
  "dom_id": "step-e6106",
  "name": "Example: Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Multiplicative Property",
  "problem": "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R} xy\\ \\!e^{x+y}\\ \\textrm d A$ over the rectangle $R= [0,1] \\times [1,2].$",
  "worked_solution": "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\iint\\limits_{R}  xy\\  e^{x+y}\\: \\textrm d A &= \\iint\\limits_{R} \\Big( x\\ \\! e^x \\Big)\\Big( y\\ \\! e^{y} \\Big) \\textrm d A\\[5pt]\n&= \\left(\\int_0^1x\\  e^{x}  \\ \\textrm d x\\right)\\left( \\int_1^2 y \\ \\!e^{y} \\ \\textrm d y\\right)\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &= \\Big[x\\ \\!e^x-e^x\\Big]_0^1 \\cdot  \\Big[y\\ \\!e^y-e^y\\Big]_1^2\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &=  \\Big(e^1-e^1 - \\left(0-e^0\\right)\\Big) \\cdot \\Big(2e^2-e^2 - \\left(e^1-e^1\\right) \\Big)\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &= 1\\cdot e^2\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &= e^2\n}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
